WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.160
In the late Ming dynasty, the Later Jin power gradually rose in the north, and alarms from the frontier kept coming.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:12.560
Thick black smoke rose from the beacon tower, carrying the message far away.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.200
The fighting in Liaodong grew fiercer by the day, and the soldiers defending the city all stood ready in strict formation.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.560
General Yuan Chonghuan was ordered to defend Ningyuan; he climbed the city wall and carefully inspected the defenses.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.600
He patted the cold city wall with his hand and nodded encouragement to the soldiers.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.800
The soldiers wheeled heavy cannons into place and stood neatly on top of the high city wall.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.600
The heavy cannon muzzles pointed beyond the city, and the soldiers waited tensely.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:44.400
Smoke rose in the distance beyond the city, and the banners on the wall fluttered in the cold wind.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.600
The red flags on the city wall waved in the wind, and the defending soldiers did not leave their posts for a single step.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.400
Later, Yuan Chonghuan fell under suspicion and died, and later generations often discuss his achievements and the injustice he suffered.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.600
In the sunset, the city wall stood quietly, guarding the northern frontier.
